CARE (Canonicalization, Attribution, and Resolution Engine)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Paper:  "CARE: Pre-Execution Command Verification for Shell-Executing LLM
        Agents", Yu Liu, Wenxiao Zhang, Zhiwei Yang, Zhongyi Zhang, Hanqi
        Feng, Xinyu Wang, Peng Qiu, Yanbing Liu, Barnabas Poczos,
        Jin B. Hong. arXiv:2607.21642 (2026).
Code:   https://github.com/prisma-research/CARE
Commit: e8166db0c39fa058285b203305649a13eb31fc0b
License: MIT — Copyright (c) 2026 CARE authors

The file `data/rule_provenance.json` is vendored verbatim from the CARE
repository (`care/rules/rule_provenance.json` at the commit above). The
judge prompt strings in `data/judge_system.txt` and `data/judge_user.txt`
are copied verbatim from `care/resolution.py`. The lexicons, path catalogs,
scoring ladders and skip-predicate logic are transcribed from the CARE
Python sources with the deliberate divergences documented in README.md
(the FIX-/EXT- tables).

